 that still incremented diversity_held and owner rows not forced to ACCEPT, so the runner opened PR 765, which a session closed as superseded by PR 762. A cached review without harm decides as before. 0.9.0 0.9.0 GOAL-REVIEW-1 (2026-10-07, pillar autonomy, docs/ENSEMBLE-POLICY.md): before the merge runner opens or merges a code-loop pull request, one Workers AI model from a family other than the proposer's (CM_REVIEW_MODELS gpt-oss-120b, deepseek-v4-flash, llama-3.3-70b; ops_config code_goal_review_models) reads the goal and the head diff and answers implements, partial or no; "no" refuses the task with the defects it names, which reach the intake retry through CI-FEEDBACK-1. One call per head, cached in cloud_ops_events goal-review-<task>-<head>, metered as purpose goal-review; no AI binding or ops_config code_goal_review_enabled off skips it; three unreadable replies let the checks decide (recorded). Of the three tasks self-repair rescued on 2026-10-06/07, #2052's patch only passed [] to the removed deposit stage and #1815's wrote living-paper columns no migration creates and labelled a paper "proved" when its body said "proof"; no check could see either. Also 0.8.2 MERGE-VERIFY-ATTEMPTS-1 (2026-10-07, pillar autonomy): the merge runner's verify gate accepts a task that verified after SELF-REPAIR-1 retries (attempts below CM_TASK_MAX_ATTEMPTS 9, the orchestrator's MAX_ATTEMPTS * RETRY_ROUNDS, parity-tested) instead of attempts below 3; step done with no last_error stays the record of a passed verify, and the required checks still gate every merge. The old bound refused all three tasks self-repair rescued (ct_yop1itun7a9ulz #1815, ct_vdgdp57qdszmkb #2052, ct_i0b4q32jxbvia7 #2055), each a failure in code_task_success_rate_30d with a verified patch. 0.8.1 0.8.1 MVP-FOLD-NOTDEPLOYED-1 (2026-10-07, pillar core, agent_issues 2090-2094): a folded MVP component is judged by its fold host unless its own audit row still serves (SYNC, CRON_ONLY or http 200); 0.4.129 deferred